2. What BikeBank does (plain language)
BikeBank helps you track bike-related activity and estimate money you may save by cycling instead of other transport (or similar savings framing in the app).

For App Store review and early use, BikeBank is designed to work in mock mode by default:

You can explore the app with demo / local sample activity and savings data.
You are not required to create a cloud account or connect Strava to use the mock demo.
Optional features (email/password account via Supabase; Strava OAuth) may exist in the product but are not required for the mock-mode experience described here.
3. Data we collect — by mode
Apple’s App Privacy label asks what is collected (generally: sent off your device and retained). This section states what BikeBank does in each mode.

3.1 Mock mode (default — App Review / demo path)
Category	What happens
Account / email	Not collected. No cloud sign-up required.
User ID (cloud)	Not collected.
Strava / fitness from Strava	Not collected. Strava is not connected in mock mode.
Activity / savings records	Stored on your device (local storage) as demo or user-entered local records. If data never leaves the device, it is typically not “collected” for App Store nutrition-label purposes — but it still exists on-device.
Device / local storage	App preferences and local activity/savings figures may be stored on the device.
Analytics / ads / crash SDKs	UNKNOWN / not confirmed. This draft assumes no third-party advertising or tracking SDKs. If Expo or another library sends diagnostics, update this policy and the App Privacy label.
Location from the device	BikeBank (as described by product facts) does not claim to request device GPS for mock mode. Confirm before submit.
Summary (mock): Minimal personal data off-device. Primary storage is local.

3.2 Authenticated mode (optional — when Supabase email/password is configured and you sign up)
Category	What may be collected
Contact Info — Email Address	Yes — to create and sign in to your account.
Identifiers — User ID	Yes — e.g. Supabase-assigned user ID, linked to your account.
Activity / savings	May sync to Supabase when configured, so records can be stored in the cloud associated with your account.
Device / local	Local cache may still be used.
3.3 Strava-connected mode (optional — only if you choose to connect Strava)
Category	What may be collected
Fitness / activity data	Activity data you authorize BikeBank to receive from Strava (e.g. rides, distances, durations, and related activity fields Strava provides under the scopes you approve).
Location-derived data	Strava activities may include route or location-related information. BikeBank does not independently claim to be a mapping/GPS product; if Strava payloads include location-derived fields and those are stored or synced, treat that as potential location-related data. Flag: confirm what the app actually stores from Strava before publish.
Account linkage	Your BikeBank account (if signed in) may be linked to the Strava connection tokens needed to keep the link working.
You can choose not to connect Strava. Mock mode does not require it.

